WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.560
The fingerprint is the
reason the router can tell

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.825
a changed notice from
one it has already seen.

3
00:00:04.825 --> 00:00:08.900
It's a hash of the record without the
first-seen time and without itself,

4
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.272
so when a provider edits a
notice the fingerprint changes,

5
00:00:12.272 --> 00:00:16.487
and when the kit simply reads the same
notice again a week later, it doesn't.

6
00:00:16.487 --> 00:00:18.276
And a record has to be valid.

7
00:00:18.276 --> 00:00:23.155
The kit checks the schema's rules in code,
so the check runs on older PowerShell

8
00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:27.425
7 too, and the collector refuses to
write a run with an invalid record.

9
00:00:27.425 --> 00:00:29.710
Every time is stored in UTC.
